{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/yang-typescript/1794350496000-engineer-js-r1r3-fix.diff.txt collab/yang-typescript/1794350496000-engineer-js-r1r3-fix.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc\nindex 26aa7f2a..6e625ab4 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc\n@@ -1583,8 +1583,12 @@\n        ;; source exception AND argument-binding failure to it as the\n        ;; thrown condition, exactly once. The js/try handler runs only\n        ;; after the escape has completed source cleanup and restored the\n-       ;; saved handler/depth/frame state (§8.10.8), so the transfer\n-       ;; below never reuses a raise exit of a completed call. An\n+       ;; saved handler/depth/frame state (§8.10.8): restore-before-\n+       ;; transfer establishes that delivery ORDERING (the callee bridge\n+       ;; is absent while the caller's exit runs). It does not by itself\n+       ;; prove that a resumed suspension cannot reuse a completed call's\n+       ;; raise exit; that lifetime claim remains an explicit open\n+       ;; obligation pending the suspension probe. An\n        ;; unchanged rethrow of a wrapper carrying a retained protocol\n        ;; condition forwards that original condition with no new wrapper;\n        ;; every other escape (including a thrown condition-shaped map,\n@@ -1649,20 +1653,42 @@\n     ;; §8.10.7 protocol reception: :yang.call/not-callable,\n     ;; :yang.call/invalid-invocation and :yang.call/unsupported-binding map\n     ;; to a local TypeError that RETAINS the complete original condition\n-    ;; (qualified reason AND plain evidence) in private cell contents,\n-    ;; outside source-writable :props. An unchanged rethrow of the same\n-    ;; wrapper forwards the original condition through the entry bridge\n-    ;; with no new wrapper. Otherwise-foreign :yang.call/thrown payloads\n-    ;; are delivered raw (the ruling's js allowance). A returned\n-    ;; condition-shaped map stays ordinary data, and forged or\n-    ;; source-writable attributes never authenticate a retained condition.\n+    ;; (qualified reason AND plain evidence) in a runtime-owned companion\n+    ;; provenance cell, outside source-writable :props. The companion\n+    ;; holds the condition, a back-reference to this exact wrapper cell,\n+    ;; and the task's retained seal: a cell js/init! allocates whose\n+    ;; reference no js definition returns, so admitted source cannot\n+    ;; obtain it. The wrapper holds only the companion reference.\n+    ;; js/retained-condition authenticates all of it: heap-authentic\n+    ;; wrapper and companion, the companion's wrapper identical (=) to\n+    ;; the candidate, and its seal identical to the runtime's. A minted\n+    ;; cell cannot replicate the seal, and a copy of the wrapper's\n+    ;; contents into a new cell fails the identity back-reference, so\n+    ;; neither authenticates a retained condition (R5). The companion is\n+    ;; reachable only through the wrapper, so the association lives\n+    ;; exactly as long as the wrapper does, with no ambient registry.\n+    ;; An unchanged rethrow of the same wrapper forwards the original\n+    ;; condition through the entry bridge with no new wrapper.\n+    ;; Otherwise-foreign :yang.call/thrown payloads are delivered raw\n+    ;; (the ruling's js allowance). A returned condition-shaped map stays\n+    ;; ordinary data.\n     [js/retained-condition\n      (fn [e]\n        (if (js/cell? e)\n          (if (cell/authentic? e)\n            (let [c (cell/get e)]\n              (if (= (get c :js/class) :error)\n-               (get c :yang.call/retained-condition)\n+               (let [p (get c :yang.call/retained-provenance)]\n+                 (if (js/cell? p)\n+                   (if (cell/authentic? p)\n+                     (let [pc (cell/get p)]\n+                       (if (= (get pc :yang.call/wrapper) e)\n+                         (if (= (get pc :yang.call/seal) js.rt/retained-seal)\n+                           (get pc :yang.call/condition)\n+                           nil)\n+                         nil))\n+                     nil)\n+                   nil))\n                nil))\n            nil)\n          nil))]\n@@ -1676,8 +1702,15 @@\n                    (if (= reason :yang.call/unsupported-binding)\n                      {:js/str \"unsupported binding profile\"}\n                      {:js/str \"invalid function invocation\"})))]\n-         (do (cell/set! e (assoc (cell/get e)\n-                                 :yang.call/retained-condition condition))\n+         (do (cell/set! e\n+                        (assoc (cell/get e)\n+                               :yang.call/retained-provenance\n+                               (cell/new\n+                                 (assoc (assoc (assoc {}\n+                                                      :yang.call/wrapper e)\n+                                               :yang.call/seal\n+                                               js.rt/retained-seal)\n+                                        :yang.call/condition condition))))\n              (js/throw e))))]\n     [js/call\n      (fn [f this args]\n@@ -4097,6 +4130,7 @@\n         ['do\n          (define 'js.rt/ctx '(cell/new (js/ctx nil)))\n          (define 'js.rt/out '(cell/new []))\n+         (define 'js.rt/retained-seal '(cell/new :js/retained-seal))\n          (define 'js.rt/obj-proto '(js/make-object :js/null))\n          (define 'js.rt/fn-proto '(js/make-object js.rt/obj-proto))\n          (define 'js.rt/global '(js/make-object js.rt/obj-proto))]\n@@ -4256,7 +4290,7 @@\n (def runtime-keys\n   \"Every key `js/init!` allocates, the ready flag aside, sorted.\"\n   (vec (sort-by str\n-                (concat '[js.rt/ctx js.rt/out js.rt/global js.rt/obj-proto\n+                (concat '[js.rt/ctx js.rt/out js.rt/retained-seal js.rt/global js.rt/obj-proto\n                           js.rt/fn-proto js.rt/symbol-proto js.rt/array-proto]\n                         (map second error-classes)\n                         (map first primitive-protos)))))\ndiff --git a/test/yang/call/exception_contract_test.clj b/test/yang/call/exception_contract_test.clj\nindex 9c3bf10b..c5ac50ec 100644\n--- a/test/yang/call/exception_contract_test.clj\n+++ b/test/yang/call/exception_contract_test.clj\n@@ -54,3 +54,31 @@\n            :frontends #{:clojure}}\n   clojure-provenance-test\n   (check-frontend :clojure))\n+\n+\n+(deftest ^{:slow true :gates #{::contract/r5} :frontends #{:typescript}}\n+  typescript-minted-forgery-test\n+  ;; A source-minted error-looking cell (and a companion-layout mimic with\n+  ;; an attacker-chosen seal) thrown through the donor's raise_value must\n+  ;; NOT forward its forged condition: the bridge delivers a fresh\n+  ;; :yang.call/thrown carrying the minted cell itself.\n+  (doseq [[backend actual] (probes/run-typescript-forgery :minted)]\n+    (if (instance? Throwable actual)\n+      (do-report {:type :error :message (str \"minted forgery \" backend \" operational failure\")\n+                  :expected {:minted-refused true :mimic-refused true} :actual actual})\n+      (is (= {:minted-refused true :mimic-refused true} actual)\n+          (str \"minted forgery \" backend)))))\n+\n+\n+(deftest ^{:slow true :gates #{::contract/r5} :frontends #{:typescript}}\n+  typescript-copied-wrapper-forgery-test\n+  ;; A fresh cell carrying a copy of a genuine protocol wrapper's complete\n+  ;; contents, thrown from another activation, must NOT forward the\n+  ;; original condition: provenance is bound to the genuine wrapper's\n+  ;; identity, not to its copyable contents.\n+  (doseq [[backend actual] (probes/run-typescript-forgery :copied)]\n+    (if (instance? Throwable actual)\n+      (do-report {:type :error :message (str \"copied wrapper \" backend \" operational failure\")\n+                  :expected {:retained true :copy-refused true} :actual actual})\n+      (is (= {:retained true :copy-refused true} actual)\n+          (str \"copied wrapper \" backend)))))\ndiff --git a/test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj b/test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj\nindex bedb3abc..fe51dc7d 100644\n--- a/test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj\n+++ b/test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj\n@@ -158,6 +158,91 @@\n         :else (throw (ex-info \"unknown provenance fixture\" {:scenario scenario}))))))\n \n \n+(defn- refused-as-thrown?\n+  \"Guest form: the boundary result refused retained-condition forwarding —\n+   one raise carrying a fresh :yang.call/thrown whose payload is `thrown`\n+   itself, never the forged condition.\"\n+  [result thrown]\n+  (list 'if (list '= :raise (list 'get result :route))\n+        (list 'if (list '= 1 (list 'get result :transfers))\n+              (list 'if (list '= :yang.call/thrown (reason result))\n+                    (list '= thrown (payload result))\n+                    false)\n+              false)\n+        false))\n+\n+\n+(defn forgery-observation-form\n+  \"The architect's two R5 forgery probes against the TypeScript donor.\n+   :minted — admitted Clojure source mints an error-looking cell (and a\n+   second cell mimicking a companion-provenance layout with an\n+   attacker-chosen seal) and throws each through the donor's raise_value.\n+   :copied — the probe copies a genuine protocol wrapper's complete cell\n+   contents into a fresh cell and throws the copy from a new activation.\n+   Both must refuse: a fresh :yang.call/thrown carrying the thrown cell\n+   itself as payload, never the forged/original condition forwarded.\"\n+  [kind]\n+  (let [export #(read-export :typescript %)\n+        forged-condition {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable\n+                          :yang.call/data {:forged true}}]\n+    (kit/guard-exceptions-form\n+      [:python :typescript]\n+      (case kind\n+        :minted\n+        (list 'let ['forged (list 'cell/new\n+                                  (list 'assoc\n+                                        (list 'assoc\n+                                              (list 'assoc {} :js/type :object)\n+                                              :js/class :error)\n+                                        :yang.call/retained-condition forged-condition))\n+                    'minted-result (call (export \"raise_value\") ['forged])\n+                    'wannabe (list 'cell/new\n+                                   (list 'assoc\n+                                         (list 'assoc {} :js/type :object)\n+                                         :js/class :error))\n+                    'companion (list 'cell/new\n+                                     (list 'assoc\n+                                           (list 'assoc\n+                                                 (list 'assoc {}\n+                                                       :yang.call/wrapper 'wannabe)\n+                                                 :yang.call/seal (list 'cell/new :attacker-seal))\n+                                           :yang.call/condition forged-condition))\n+                    'armed (list 'do\n+                                 (list 'cell/set! 'wannabe\n+                                       (list 'assoc (list 'cell/get 'wannabe)\n+                                             :yang.call/retained-provenance 'companion))\n+                                 'wannabe)\n+                    'mimic-result (call (export \"raise_value\") ['armed])]\n+              (kit/observation-map-form\n+                {:minted-refused (refused-as-thrown? 'minted-result 'forged)\n+                 :mimic-refused (refused-as-thrown? 'mimic-result 'armed)}))\n+        :copied\n+        (list 'let ['probe.condition (protocol-condition :yang.call/not-callable)\n+                    'probe.injected (injected 'probe.condition)\n+                    'retained (call (export \"retain\") ['probe.injected])\n+                    'wrapper (list 'get 'retained :value)\n+                    'copy (list 'cell/new (list 'cell/get 'wrapper))\n+                    'result (call (export \"raise_value\") ['copy])]\n+              (kit/observation-map-form\n+                {:retained (list '= :return (list 'get 'retained :route))\n+                 :copy-refused (refused-as-thrown? 'result 'copy)}))))))\n+\n+\n+(defn run-typescript-forgery\n+  \"Run one forgery probe kind against the TypeScript donor on all three\n+   linked vector VMs; answers {backend observation}.\"\n+  [kind]\n+  (try\n+    (let [donor @boundary-donor]\n+      (kit/run-exception-program\n+        donor\n+        (kit/compose-exception donor [\"boundary_target\"] :typescript\n+                               (contract/sources :typescript)\n+                               (forgery-observation-form kind))))\n+    (catch Throwable e\n+      (kit/error-results e))))\n+\n+\n (defn run-fixture\n   \"One source-created receiver per task. All three linked vector VMs run.\n    A fresh task prevents a deliberately broken bridge from poisoning the\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-10 23:07:50 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-11 06:07:50 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\nCoding-Agent: interactive (Muse Code / muse-wonder-1.0 — yang.typescript engineer seat)\nSession-ID: 16702856-c19f-4543-9864-6af13d6bf46b\n\n# Findings: JS R1+R3 fix round — retained-condition provenance (P1 closed, P2 narrowed)\n\nBranch `exception-js-r1r3`, commit `ce99e65e` (`fix(yang.typescript):\nauthenticate retained-condition provenance against minted forgeries`) on top\nof `c0114a42`. Not merged, not pushed, master untouched.\n\n## Mechanism chosen, and why a minted cell cannot replicate it\n\nCompanion provenance cell + runtime seal + wrapper-identity back-reference,\nall allocated by the runtime at protocol-reception time; no registry.\n\n- `js/raise-protocol` (`prelude.cljc:1695`) still builds the local TypeError\n  wrapper `e` via `js/make-error`. It no longer writes the condition into the\n  wrapper's own contents. It allocates a fresh companion cell holding\n  `{:yang.call/wrapper e, :yang.call/seal js.rt/retained-seal,\n  :yang.call/condition condition}` and writes only the companion reference\n  into the wrapper under `:yang.call/retained-provenance` (:1707-1713),\n  then throws `e`.\n- `js.rt/retained-seal` (:4133, init-form; registered in `runtime-keys`\n  :4293) is a cell `js/init!` allocates once per task. No `js/` definition\n  returns it or its contents; JS source has no name for it and the Clojure\n  donor/probe sources run under their own prelude namespace. Admitted\n  source therefore cannot obtain the seal reference to stamp into a forged\n  companion.\n- `js/retained-condition` (:1675-1694) now authenticates, in order: the\n  candidate is a cell and `cell/authentic?`; its contents are\n  `:js/class :error`; `:yang.call/retained-provenance` is a cell and\n  `cell/authentic?`; the companion's `:yang.call/wrapper` is identical\n  (`=`, cell-reference identity) to the candidate; its `:yang.call/seal`\n  is identical to `js.rt/retained-seal`. Only then does it answer the\n  companion's `:yang.call/condition`. Every other shape answers nil, and\n  the entry bridge (:1617) delivers a fresh `:yang.call/thrown` carrying\n  the thrown value itself.\n\nWhy each attack fails: (1) a minted cell from scratch (the architect's\n`cell/new` snippet, or a mimic that builds its own companion layout) has\nno companion the runtime sealed — an attacker-chosen seal cell is not\nidentical to `js.rt/retained-seal`, and the old\n`:yang.call/retained-condition` contents key is no longer read at all.\n(2) A copied-metadata wrapper carries the genuine companion reference,\nbut the companion's back-reference names the genuine wrapper cell, not\nthe copy, so the identity check refuses. Lifetime: the companion is\nreachable only through the wrapper, so the association lives exactly as\nlong as the wrapper (survives `retain`/`later` across activations, as the\nunchanged 30/30 provenance gate confirms) and needs no ambient/global\ntable; per-task state is limited to the one seal cell from `js/init!`.\n\nP2: the bridge comment (:1584-1592) now claims only that\nrestore-before-transfer establishes delivery ORDERING (the callee bridge\nis absent while the caller's exit runs), and names the no-reuse-after-\ncompletion lifetime claim an explicit open obligation pending the\nsuspension probe. Standing rulings respected: no nil-raise-exit guest\nfallback added; no common-constructor claim for `js/construct-with-nt`;\nthe `exception_contract.clj:55` donor tweak untouched.\n\n## Exact diff hunks (commit ce99e65e, 3 files, +160/-13)\n\n- `src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:1584-1592` — P2 comment\n  narrowing (above).\n- `src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:1653-1694` — retention\n  section comment rewritten; `js/retained-condition` replaced with the\n  five-step authentication (above); the `:yang.call/retained-condition`\n  contents key is gone.\n- `src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:1695-1714` —\n  `js/raise-protocol` allocates the sealed companion and stores only its\n  reference on the wrapper.\n- `src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:4133` —\n  `(define 'js.rt/retained-seal '(cell/new :js/retained-seal))` in\n  `js/init!`, beside `js.rt/ctx`/`js.rt/out`.\n- `src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:4293` —\n  `js.rt/retained-seal` added to `runtime-keys` (module placeholder).\n- `test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj` (+85) — `refused-as-thrown?`,\n  `forgery-observation-form`, `run-typescript-forgery`.\n- `test/yang/call/exception_contract_test.clj:59-84` (+28) — the two new\n  deftests below. No existing fixture, expectation, or count changed.\n\n## The two new probes, with refusal evidence\n\nBoth run the real TypeScript donor source (`retain`/`raise_value` from\n`exception_contract.clj`) composed by the kit on all three VMs\n(semantic/stack/register), assertions guest-side in the probe program.\n\n1. `typescript-minted-forgery-test` — probe Clojure source mints (a) the\n   architect's error-looking cell carrying\n   `:yang.call/retained-condition {:yang.call/reason\n   :yang.call/not-callable, :yang.call/data {:forged true}}`, and (b) a\n   mimic wrapper armed with an attacker-built companion (own seal cell,\n   back-reference, forged condition). Each is thrown through the donor's\n   `raise_value`. Expected and observed post-fix:\n   `{:minted-refused true, :mimic-refused true}` on every backend —\n   one raise, fresh `:yang.call/thrown`, payload identical to the minted\n   cell itself; the forged condition never forwards.\n2. `typescript-copied-wrapper-forgery-test` — probe obtains a genuine\n   protocol wrapper via `retain` on an injected\n   `:yang.call/not-callable` condition, copies its complete cell contents\n   with `(cell/new (cell/get wrapper))`, and throws the copy through\n   `raise_value` from a new activation. Expected and observed post-fix:\n   `{:retained true, :copy-refused true}` on every backend.\n\nPre-fix evidence (same probes, before the prelude edit): 6 failures,\n0 errors — `{:minted-refused false, :mimic-refused true}` and\n`{:retained true, :copy-refused false}` on all three VMs, i.e. the\nminted cell and the copied wrapper both forwarded their conditions\n(the executed P1 reproduction). Post-fix: `Ran 2 tests containing 6\nassertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.`\n\n## Exact commands run, with assertion counts (laptop, focused only)\n\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.call.exception-contract-test -v .../typescript-minted-forgery-test -v .../typescript-copied-wrapper-forgery-test`\n  → pre-fix 6 failures (above); post-fix `Ran 2 tests containing 6\n  assertions`, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.call.exception-contract-test -v yang.call.exception-contract-test/typescript-provenance-test`\n  → `Ran 1 tests containing 30 assertions`, 0 failures, 0 errors (30/30;\n  all `saved-protocol-*` and `shape-*` rows stay green, so genuine\n  retained wrappers still forward their complete original conditions).\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.call.conformance-test -n yang.call.exception-source-test`\n  → `Ran 6 tests containing 131 assertions`, 0 failures, 0 errors (6/131).\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.typescript.antlr.source-call-test`\n  → `Ran 2 tests containing 22 assertions`, 0 failures, 0 errors (2/22).\n- `clojure -M -e \"(require 'yang.typescript.antlr.prelude) ...\"` → loads\n  clean; `js.rt/retained-seal` present in `runtime-keys`.\n- No suite-scale run, no Node/Dart legs (per round surface).\n\n## Weakening / deferral I could not avoid\n\n- Residual surface, stated plainly: an attacker who already holds a\n  genuine wrapper and deliberately reads its companion with raw\n  `cell/get` can extract the seal reference and the condition, and a\n  deliberate in-place `cell/set!` of a genuine companion is not detected.\n  The two architect-required probes (mint-from-scratch, copy-to-new-cell)\n  both refuse, and no wrapper-riding scheme can do better while admitted\n  source holds raw `cell/get`/`cell/set!` over a wrapper it legitimately\n  possesses; the only stronger shape is a runtime registry keyed by\n  wrapper identity, which the architect explicitly ruled out. I did not\n  add an extraction-from-genuine-companion probe, since it would encode\n  this known residual as a failing expectation rather than a contract\n  the fix claims.\n- The suspension/raise-exit lifetime probe remains a named open\n  obligation (now stated in the :1586 comment), as the architect ruled;\n  generator/async lowering still refuses, so it is not closable in this\n  round.\n- Nothing else weakened: no existing assertion, fixture, or gate count\n  changed; `js/call`, the entry bridge, and the donor sources are\n  untouched apart from the hunks listed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
