{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc | sed -n '1577,1738p;4115,4148p;4278,4315p'; nl -ba test/yang/call/exception_contract_test.clj | sed -n '50,100p'; rg -n 'forg|provenance|retained-seal' test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj\"","aggregated_output":"  1577\t    [js/make-function-nt\n  1578\t     (fn [name length this-mode kind code nt?]\n  1579\t       ;; Ordinary calls enter through yang.call; construction still applies\n  1580\t       ;; the private code with its explicit new.target below.\n  1581\t       ;; §8.10.7 callee bridge: installed BEFORE argument binding, it\n  1582\t       ;; reads the supplied :yang.call/raise and delivers every escaping\n  1583\t       ;; source exception AND argument-binding failure to it as the\n  1584\t       ;; thrown condition, exactly once. The js/try handler runs only\n  1585\t       ;; after the escape has completed source cleanup and restored the\n  1586\t       ;; saved handler/depth/frame state (§8.10.8): restore-before-\n  1587\t       ;; transfer establishes that delivery ORDERING (the callee bridge\n  1588\t       ;; is absent while the caller's exit runs). It does not by itself\n  1589\t       ;; prove that a resumed suspension cannot reuse a completed call's\n  1590\t       ;; raise exit; that lifetime claim remains an explicit open\n  1591\t       ;; obligation pending the suspension probe. An\n  1592\t       ;; unchanged rethrow of a wrapper carrying a retained protocol\n  1593\t       ;; condition forwards that original condition with no new wrapper;\n  1594\t       ;; every other escape (including a thrown condition-shaped map,\n  1595\t       ;; which is the payload of a FRESH condition per §8.10.7) becomes\n  1596\t       ;; :yang.call/thrown carrying the original value.\n  1597\t       (let [entry\n  1598\t             (fn [invocation]\n  1599\t               (let [raise-exit (get invocation :yang.call/raise)]\n  1600\t                 (js/try\n  1601\t                   (fn []\n  1602\t                     (let [callee (get invocation :yang.call/callee)\n  1603\t                           c (cell/get callee)\n  1604\t                           k (get c :kind)\n  1605\t                           receiver (if (data/contains? invocation :yang.call/receiver)\n  1606\t                                      (get invocation :yang.call/receiver)\n  1607\t                                      :js/undefined)]\n  1608\t                       (if (if (= k :class) true (= k :derived))\n  1609\t                         (js/throw-type-error\n  1610\t                           {:js/str \"Class constructor cannot be invoked without 'new'\"})\n  1611\t                         (let [t (if (= (get c :this-mode) :lexical) :js/undefined receiver)\n  1612\t                               args (get invocation :yang.call/positional)]\n  1613\t                           (if (= (get c :nt?) true)\n  1614\t                             ((get c :code) t args :js/undefined)\n  1615\t                             ((get c :code) t args))))))\n  1616\t                   (fn [e]\n  1617\t                     (let [retained (js/retained-condition e)]\n  1618\t                       (if (nil? retained)\n  1619\t                         (raise-exit (assoc (assoc {} :yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown)\n  1620\t                                            :yang.call/value e))\n  1621\t                         (raise-exit retained)))))))]\n  1622\t         (let [f (cell/new\n  1623\t                   (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc {}\n  1624\t                                                                                                :js/type\n  1625\t                                                                                                :function)\n  1626\t                                                                                         :code code)\n  1627\t                                                                                  :yang.call/entry entry)\n  1628\t                                                                           :this-mode this-mode)\n  1629\t                                                                    :name name)\n  1630\t                                                             :length length)\n  1631\t                                                      :props (js/om-new))\n  1632\t                                               :proto js.rt/fn-proto)\n  1633\t                                        :extensible? true)\n  1634\t                                 :kind\n  1635\t                                 kind)\n  1636\t                          :nt?\n  1637\t                          nt?))]\n  1638\t           (do (js/define-own! f\n  1639\t                               {:js/str \"length\"}\n  1640\t                               (js/slot (data/float64 length) false false true))\n  1641\t               (js/define-own! f {:js/str \"name\"} (js/slot name false false true))\n  1642\t               (if (= kind :normal)\n  1643\t                 (let [p (js/make-object js.rt/obj-proto)]\n  1644\t                   (do (js/define-own! f\n  1645\t                                       {:js/str \"prototype\"}\n  1646\t                                       (js/slot p true false false))\n  1647\t                       (js/define-own! p\n  1648\t                                       {:js/str \"constructor\"}\n  1649\t                                       (js/slot f true false true))))\n  1650\t                 :js/undefined)\n  1651\t               f))))]\n  1652\t    ;; ------------------------------------------- protocol-condition retention\n  1653\t    ;; §8.10.7 protocol reception: :yang.call/not-callable,\n  1654\t    ;; :yang.call/invalid-invocation and :yang.call/unsupported-binding map\n  1655\t    ;; to a local TypeError that RETAINS the complete original condition\n  1656\t    ;; (qualified reason AND plain evidence) in a runtime-owned companion\n  1657\t    ;; provenance cell, outside source-writable :props. The companion\n  1658\t    ;; holds the condition, a back-reference to this exact wrapper cell,\n  1659\t    ;; and the task's retained seal: a cell js/init! allocates whose\n  1660\t    ;; reference no js definition returns, so admitted source cannot\n  1661\t    ;; obtain it. The wrapper holds only the companion reference.\n  1662\t    ;; js/retained-condition authenticates all of it: heap-authentic\n  1663\t    ;; wrapper and companion, the companion's wrapper identical (=) to\n  1664\t    ;; the candidate, and its seal identical to the runtime's. A minted\n  1665\t    ;; cell cannot replicate the seal, and a copy of the wrapper's\n  1666\t    ;; contents into a new cell fails the identity back-reference, so\n  1667\t    ;; neither authenticates a retained condition (R5). The companion is\n  1668\t    ;; reachable only through the wrapper, so the association lives\n  1669\t    ;; exactly as long as the wrapper does, with no ambient registry.\n  1670\t    ;; An unchanged rethrow of the same wrapper forwards the original\n  1671\t    ;; condition through the entry bridge with no new wrapper.\n  1672\t    ;; Otherwise-foreign :yang.call/thrown payloads are delivered raw\n  1673\t    ;; (the ruling's js allowance). A returned condition-shaped map stays\n  1674\t    ;; ordinary data.\n  1675\t    [js/retained-condition\n  1676\t     (fn [e]\n  1677\t       (if (js/cell? e)\n  1678\t         (if (cell/authentic? e)\n  1679\t           (let [c (cell/get e)]\n  1680\t             (if (= (get c :js/class) :error)\n  1681\t               (let [p (get c :yang.call/retained-provenance)]\n  1682\t                 (if (js/cell? p)\n  1683\t                   (if (cell/authentic? p)\n  1684\t                     (let [pc (cell/get p)]\n  1685\t                       (if (= (get pc :yang.call/wrapper) e)\n  1686\t                         (if (= (get pc :yang.call/seal) js.rt/retained-seal)\n  1687\t                           (get pc :yang.call/condition)\n  1688\t                           nil)\n  1689\t                         nil))\n  1690\t                     nil)\n  1691\t                   nil))\n  1692\t               nil))\n  1693\t           nil)\n  1694\t         nil))]\n  1695\t    [js/raise-protocol\n  1696\t     (fn [condition]\n  1697\t       (let [reason (get condition :yang.call/reason)\n  1698\t             e (js/make-error\n  1699\t                 js.rt/type-error-proto\n  1700\t                 (if (= reason :yang.call/not-callable)\n  1701\t                   {:js/str \"value is not a function\"}\n  1702\t                   (if (= reason :yang.call/unsupported-binding)\n  1703\t                     {:js/str \"unsupported binding profile\"}\n  1704\t                     {:js/str \"invalid function invocation\"})))]\n  1705\t         (do (cell/set! e\n  1706\t                        (assoc (cell/get e)\n  1707\t                               :yang.call/retained-provenance\n  1708\t                               (cell/new\n  1709\t                                 (assoc (assoc (assoc {}\n  1710\t                                                      :yang.call/wrapper e)\n  1711\t                                               :yang.call/seal\n  1712\t                                               js.rt/retained-seal)\n  1713\t                                        :yang.call/condition condition))))\n  1714\t             (js/throw e))))]\n  1715\t    [js/call\n  1716\t     (fn [f this args]\n  1717\t       (yang.call/invoke-with\n  1718\t         f args []\n  1719\t         (fn [condition]\n  1720\t           (if (= (get condition :yang.call/reason) :yang.call/thrown)\n  1721\t             (js/throw (get condition :yang.call/value))\n  1722\t             (js/raise-protocol condition)))\n  1723\t         (assoc {} :yang.call/receiver this)))]\n  1724\t    [js/is-constructor?\n  1725\t     ;; [[Construct]] exists on :normal functions, class constructors and the\n  1726\t     ;; builtins flagged :ctor?; arrows, methods, accessors and the rest have\n  1727\t     ;; none\n  1728\t     (fn [v]\n  1729\t       (if (js/callable? v)\n  1730\t         (let [c (cell/get v)\n  1731\t               k (get c :kind)]\n  1732\t           (if (= k :normal)\n  1733\t             true\n  1734\t             (if (= k :class)\n  1735\t               true\n  1736\t               (if (= k :derived)\n  1737\t                 true\n  1738\t                 (if (= k :builtin) (= (get c :ctor?) true) false)))))\n  4115\t\n  4116\t\n  4117\t(defn- init-form\n  4118\t  \"`js/init!`'s body: the context and out cells, the prototypes in\n  4119\t   dependency order (`%Object.prototype%`, `%Function.prototype%`, then the\n  4120\t   rest), the intrinsic methods, the Error family, the global object and\n  4121\t   its bindings, then the ready flag, under the uninit guard.\"\n  4122\t  []\n  4123\t  (list\n  4124\t    'fn\n  4125\t    []\n  4126\t    (list\n  4127\t      'if\n  4128\t      (list '= 'js.rt/state :js/uninit)\n  4129\t      (concat\n  4130\t        ['do\n  4131\t         (define 'js.rt/ctx '(cell/new (js/ctx nil)))\n  4132\t         (define 'js.rt/out '(cell/new []))\n  4133\t         (define 'js.rt/retained-seal '(cell/new :js/retained-seal))\n  4134\t         (define 'js.rt/obj-proto '(js/make-object :js/null))\n  4135\t         (define 'js.rt/fn-proto '(js/make-object js.rt/obj-proto))\n  4136\t         (define 'js.rt/global '(js/make-object js.rt/obj-proto))]\n  4137\t        [(define 'js.rt/error-proto '(js/make-object js.rt/obj-proto))]\n  4138\t        (mapv (fn [[_ key base]] (define key (list 'js/make-object base)))\n  4139\t              (rest error-classes))\n  4140\t        (mapv (fn [[key _ _]] (define key '(js/make-object js.rt/obj-proto)))\n  4141\t              primitive-protos)\n  4142\t        [(define 'js.rt/symbol-proto '(js/make-object js.rt/obj-proto))\n  4143\t         (define 'js.rt/array-proto '(js/make-object js.rt/obj-proto))]\n  4144\t        (mapcat (fn [[proto ms]]\n  4145\t                  (mapv (fn [[nm n code]]\n  4146\t                          (list 'js/def-method! proto nm n code))\n  4147\t                        ms))\n  4148\t                methods-of)\n  4278\t  (u/then functions-uast (u/sexp->uast '(js/init!))))\n  4279\t\n  4280\t\n  4281\t;; =============================================================================\n  4282\t;; The linked js module requires the separately published `yang.call` module\n  4283\t;; =============================================================================\n  4284\t\n  4285\t(def module-name\n  4286\t  \"The linker module the JavaScript runtime profile is published as.\"\n  4287\t  'js)\n  4288\t\n  4289\t\n  4290\t(def runtime-keys\n  4291\t  \"Every key `js/init!` allocates, the ready flag aside, sorted.\"\n  4292\t  (vec (sort-by str\n  4293\t                (concat '[js.rt/ctx js.rt/out js.rt/retained-seal js.rt/global js.rt/obj-proto\n  4294\t                          js.rt/fn-proto js.rt/symbol-proto js.rt/array-proto]\n  4295\t                        (map second error-classes)\n  4296\t                        (map first primitive-protos)))))\n  4297\t\n  4298\t\n  4299\t(defn strip\n  4300\t  \"`sym` without the module's own namespace `js`; any other value as it\n  4301\t   is. `js.rt/*` stays qualified: an internal store key.\"\n  4302\t  [sym]\n  4303\t  (core/strip \"js\" sym))\n  4304\t\n  4305\t\n  4306\t(def ^:private module-definitions\n  4307\t  \"The module's definition list: a `:js/uninit` placeholder for every\n  4308\t   runtime key, then every definition, stripped.\"\n  4309\t  (core/module-definitions \"js\" :js/uninit runtime-keys linked-definitions))\n  4310\t\n  4311\t\n  4312\t(def module-uast\n  4313\t  \"The module tree: one application whose operands are the definitions, in\n  4314\t   order, applied to a lambda that returns nil.\"\n  4315\t  (core/module-tree module-definitions []))\n    50\t  (check-frontend :typescript))\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t(deftest ^{:slow true :gates #{::contract/r1 ::contract/r3 ::contract/r5}\n    54\t           :frontends #{:clojure}}\n    55\t  clojure-provenance-test\n    56\t  (check-frontend :clojure))\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\t(deftest ^{:slow true :gates #{::contract/r5} :frontends #{:typescript}}\n    60\t  typescript-minted-forgery-test\n    61\t  ;; A source-minted error-looking cell (and a companion-layout mimic with\n    62\t  ;; an attacker-chosen seal) thrown through the donor's raise_value must\n    63\t  ;; NOT forward its forged condition: the bridge delivers a fresh\n    64\t  ;; :yang.call/thrown carrying the minted cell itself.\n    65\t  (doseq [[backend actual] (probes/run-typescript-forgery :minted)]\n    66\t    (if (instance? Throwable actual)\n    67\t      (do-report {:type :error :message (str \"minted forgery \" backend \" operational failure\")\n    68\t                  :expected {:minted-refused true :mimic-refused true} :actual actual})\n    69\t      (is (= {:minted-refused true :mimic-refused true} actual)\n    70\t          (str \"minted forgery \" backend)))))\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\t(deftest ^{:slow true :gates #{::contract/r5} :frontends #{:typescript}}\n    74\t  typescript-copied-wrapper-forgery-test\n    75\t  ;; A fresh cell carrying a copy of a genuine protocol wrapper's complete\n    76\t  ;; contents, thrown from another activation, must NOT forward the\n    77\t  ;; original condition: provenance is bound to the genuine wrapper's\n    78\t  ;; identity, not to its copyable contents.\n    79\t  (doseq [[backend actual] (probes/run-typescript-forgery :copied)]\n    80\t    (if (instance? Throwable actual)\n    81\t      (do-report {:type :error :message (str \"copied wrapper \" backend \" operational failure\")\n    82\t                  :expected {:retained true :copy-refused true} :actual actual})\n    83\t      (is (= {:retained true :copy-refused true} actual)\n    84\t          (str \"copied wrapper \" backend)))))\n84:        (#{:fresh-named :fresh-closure :forged-retention} scenario)\n85:        (list 'let [original (list 'get (call (export (if (= scenario :forged-retention)\n86:                                                        \"forged\" \"payload\"))\n87:                                              (if (= scenario :forged-retention)\n93:                             :forged-retention (call (export \"raise_value\") [original]))]\n158:        :else (throw (ex-info \"unknown provenance fixture\" {:scenario scenario}))))))\n164:   itself, never the forged condition.\"\n175:(defn forgery-observation-form\n176:  \"The architect's two R5 forgery probes against the TypeScript donor.\n178:   second cell mimicking a companion-provenance layout with an\n183:   itself as payload, never the forged/original condition forwarded.\"\n186:        forged-condition {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable\n187:                          :yang.call/data {:forged true}}]\n192:        (list 'let ['forged (list 'cell/new\n197:                                        :yang.call/retained-condition forged-condition))\n198:                    'minted-result (call (export \"raise_value\") ['forged])\n209:                                           :yang.call/condition forged-condition))\n213:                                             :yang.call/retained-provenance 'companion))\n217:                {:minted-refused (refused-as-thrown? 'minted-result 'forged)\n231:(defn run-typescript-forgery\n232:  \"Run one forgery probe kind against the TypeScript donor on all three\n241:                               (forgery-observation-form kind))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,117p' collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md; sed -n '3874,3908p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; rg -n 'opaque|closure.*reflect|reflect.*closure|private.*identity|weak' docs/design/yang.antlr.md src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,117p' collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md; sed -n '3874,3908p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; rg -n 'opaque|closure.*reflect|reflect.*closure|private.*identity|weak' docs/design/yang.antlr.md src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-07 04:30:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-07 11:30:00 +07 (+0700)\nStatus: OWNER-APPROVED 2026-11-07 (\"enforce everywhere consistently. this should be a separate track.\"); v2 SUPERSEDES v1 (1794920000000) per the review round — architect gpt-6-astra, engineer mob gpt-6.1-sol + gemini-3.8-flash: all three ACCEPT WITH AMENDMENTS, folded below. Qwen aborted (headless tool denial); kimi quota-exhausted (429).\nReview records: collab/exception-track/1794930000000-architect-exception-ruling-review.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log, 1794930000000-engineer-exception-ruling-review.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log, 1794930000000-engineer-exception-ruling-review.gemini-3.8-flash.stdout.log.\n\n# RULING OF RECORD v2 — the exception track: §8.10.7 enforced uniformly in all four frontends\n\n## The decision\n\nException handling is enforced uniformly across yang.clojure, yang.typescript (js),\nyang.php, and yang.python. At every admitted guest-call boundary, an escaping source\nexception compiles down to THE SAME continuation: the caller's supplied raise exit\nreceiving the §8.10.7 condition\n\n    {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown, :yang.call/value original-thrown-value}\n\nand every receiving runtime implements the §8.10.7 reception rules as written. This is a\nSEPARATE TRACK: its own folder (collab/exception-track/), its own rounds, its own\nacceptance gate; the four frontend seats cede the exception-fix surfaces to the track and\nreceive per-frontend results back into their records.\n\n## Scope bounds (v2: sharpened per astra §5)\n\n- \"Every boundary\" means ADMITTED GUEST-CALL boundaries. VM/custody defects and host\n  implementation failures remain operational failures (design :3904); no broad\n  host catch-and-relabel is authorized.\n- A RETURNED condition-shaped map is ordinary data; a THROWN condition-shaped map is the\n  payload of a fresh condition; shape is never evidence of an existing condition to\n  forward (the cell-ref rule, restated — R5).\n- \"Same continuation\" does NOT require identical internal lowering (R4's allowance).\n\n## The requirements (v2: amended per the review round)\n\n**R1 — the callee bridge (js AND php non-compliant today).** Every frontend's published\nfunction entry, closure entry, and higher-order entry installs the exception bridge\nBEFORE argument binding: it reads the supplied `:yang.call/raise` and delivers every\nescaping source exception AND argument-binding failure to it as the thrown condition,\nexactly once, with execution after the call unreachable. js entries apply `:code` without\nreading the raise exit (prelude.cljc:1581); php's function entry (:2264) and Closure entry\n(:4217) lack it, and php's raise with an empty handler stack RETURNS normally\n(prelude.cljc:194-197). The bridge must also satisfy §8.10.8: complete cleanup and\nhandler/depth/frame restoration BEFORE the transfer; a later generator resume never\nreuses a raise exit belonging to a completed call.\n\n**R2 — foreign reception and retained-condition lifetime (python, php non-compliant\ntoday).** On receiving a thrown condition: (1) a payload valid in the receiving runtime\nkeeps its ordinary catching and identity behavior — delivered UNCHANGED (python raising\nan already-local exception raw is compliant; python raising an OTHERWISE-FOREIGN payload\nraw at :1034 is not); (2) js may deliver the otherwise-foreign payload raw; (3) python\nand php represent an otherwise-foreign payload with their own generated\n`ForeignException`, retaining the complete condition and original payload — catch-all\ncatches it, typed catches match the LOCAL hierarchy, never guessed foreign class names,\nand formatting it never implicitly invokes foreign methods. Retention rides the generated\nexception's IDENTITY for its ENTIRE LIFETIME, outside source-writable attributes, with no\nambient registry (design :3878, :3885). Raising the whole envelope (php :2384) or an\notherwise-foreign raw payload (python :1034) is non-compliant.\n\n**R3 — protocol failures retain and forward the condition (ALL FOUR frontends; v2\nwidened per astra §1 / sol §1).** `:yang.call/not-callable`, `:yang.call/invalid-invocation`,\n`:yang.call/unsupported-binding` (fully qualified) map to a documented local exception\nform retaining the complete original condition — qualified reason AND plain evidence — so\nan unchanged rethrow FORWARDS the original condition without a new wrapper. js discards\nthe condition into fresh text (:1627); python builds a generic TypeError (:1046); clojure\nretains it as catch data (:1306) but public escape reclassifies through unconditional\n`yang.call/thrown` (:1088); php constructs a fresh Error for not-callable and raises the\nenvelope otherwise (:2384), and its source rethrow rejects that envelope (:4085). All\nfour are in scope, reception AND outbound rethrow.\n\n**R4 — clojure unifies or proves equivalence.** The intra-unit outcome-token channel\n(clojure.cljc:1115, :1125-1133) may remain an optimization only with equivalence proof\nacross caught/uncaught throws, protocol rethrow, binding failures, and higher-order\nre-entry (§8.10.9's bar) — a single passing example is insufficient. Public\nprotocol-rethrow repair (R3) does not wait for this decision. Clojure's restricted catch\nsurface (single catch, no `finally`) is a source-semantics decision this ruling does not\nchange.\n\n**R5 — no new shape-routing.** Per the scope bounds above; plus: forged or\nsource-writable attributes on a wrapper-looking value never authenticate a retained\ncondition.\n\n## The baseline (audit of record)\n\nThe gpt-6.1-sol audit (collab/yang-python/1794900000000, verdict DIVERGENT, HEAD\ne9a0b430) is the baseline. Citation corrections of record from the review round: js\nfollows its GUEST continuation handler stack (js.rt/ctx, prelude.cljc:1704), not the host\nengine's; php's empty-stack return is :194-197 (envelope reception :2384); clojure's\nactual private branches are :1115 and :1125-1133 (:1110 is the packet-length guard).\n\n## Acceptance gate (v2: widened per astra §4 / sol §4)\n\nThe track is DONE when ALL of the following hold, with real source on both sides of every\nleg:\n\n1. **The directed pair matrix — 12 cross-language directions** derived from the four\n   admitted frontends (clojure↔python and clojure↔php explicitly included), plus local\n   regressions.\n2. **Callable-kind coverage**: named exports AND closure/higher-order entries (php\n   Closures concretely), supported methods/callable objects per frontend capability.\n3. **The §8.10.11 exception scenarios**: binding failures; arbitrary foreign thrown\n   data; catch-all and typed catches (where the source has them — js has no typed-catch\n   syntax, clojure's admitted surface rejects `finally`; exercise cleanup in a frontend\n   that supports it and PRESERVE clojure's rejection tests); unchanged rethrow; finally\n   replacement; protocol-error rethrow; condition-shaped thrown maps staying data;\n   A→B→A propagation asserting original identity and cleanup order; the stored\n   ForeignException rethrown from another activation.\n4. **Context lifetime**: repeated success→raise→success, cross-runtime recursion,\n   suspension/resume — handler/depth/frame state restored, exactly-once\n   binding/cleanup.\n5. **Host-by-VM results**: JVM, Node, and Dart across the admitted VM paths, with\n   explicit refusals; portable parser-produced fixtures where the JVM-only kit cannot\n   reach; bundled-walker paths where admitted, never requiring unsupported linked\n   execution; bundled/linked parity and task isolation preserving existing custody\n   refusals.\n6. **Identity assertions BEFORE rendering**: original reasons, complete evidence, payload\n   identity, wrapper non-stacking, cleanup order — equal rendered text is not identity\n   evidence.\n\n   `ForeignException`, retaining the complete condition and original\n   payload. Catch-all catches this local object. Typed source catches\n   match its local hierarchy, never guessed foreign class names.\n\n`ForeignException` is a proposed prelude-owned type, not a VM type.\nUnchanged rethrow propagates the original condition without adding\nwrappers. Raising a new exception creates a new condition. Crossing back\ninto a runtime recognizing the original exception restores its original\ntype and identity. Formatting a foreign payload must not implicitly\ninvoke a foreign method.\n\nThe runtime associates its generated wrapper's identity with the retained\ncondition for the wrapper's entire lifetime, separate from source-writable\nattributes. The association normally lives in private wrapper-cell\ncontents, or an equivalent task-owned identity structure with the same\nlifetime. It survives storing or returning the wrapper after the creating\ncall/catch activation has ended, and remains recoverable when that same\nwrapper is rethrown in another activation. Temporary catch state alone is\ninsufficient. Reachability/reclamation must retain the condition and its\npayload while the wrapper is live, without an ambient registry.\n\nThe runtime must not detect wrappers or unwrap arbitrary maps by their\nkey names. JavaScript may expose raw payloads for\n`:yang.call/thrown`; its local exception for a protocol failure must still\nretain that failure's qualified condition. Rethrowing the same generated\nexception forwards that complete condition, including protocol reasons;\nthrowing an unrelated value creates a new `:yang.call/thrown` condition.\nSaved activation state refers to this identity-owned association; exiting\nor restoring a catch does not destroy it.\n\nVM application/custody defects and host implementation failures remain\noperational failures. Do not catch them broadly and relabel them as\nsource exceptions. Existing explicit stream/module refusals keep their\nsource mappings under the relevant profiles.\n\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:984:Cursors remain opaque. Cross-host restart must not assume\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1400:| `weakref`, `__del__`, `gc`                   | 1 conforming, 3        | The reference says `__del__` is not guaranteed to run and a weakref may stay |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3603:not a signature introspection operation: Yin closures are opaque and the\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3648:It must not guess an opaque closure's signature or bypass host-effect\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3967:an opaque runtime closure proves revision compatibility. No runtime\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4272:  work after the Python spike (owner decision 4). Finalizers and weak\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4283:- Cross-language calls: a cell ref crosses as an opaque object handle.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc:22:   Both print opaquely, on every host and through `str`, `pr-str` and every\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc:38:  \"The opaque printed form of each kind, shaped like the REPL's\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
